**The EIGRP Autonomous System numbers do not match.** r11 is in AS 100; r13 is in AS 300. EIGRP neighbors will only form a relationship if they share the same AS number. After the "rollback" on r13, its configuration was restored with AS 300 instead of the correct AS 100 — causing the neighbor relationship with r11 to collapse and all 113.1.x.x prefixes to vanish from r11's EIGRP topology table.

r11 also confirms: it redistributes EIGRP into OSPF (`redistribute eigrp` inside `router ospf`), so the 113.1.x.x routes would have propagated into the wider OSPF fabric as well — they are now missing from that too.

